# Sets a new timer's duration via a CIRCULAR DRAG that winds anticlockwise
# past the dial's 0-minute mark into its "seconds windup" submode, landing
# on a duration below one minute (0:00:55) - not a single touch-and-hold at
# a fixed position (see touch_dial_set_via_position.seq for that).
#
# The gesture (touch_dial/touch.c's apply_windup): starting on the outer
# ring past the 20-minute mark, dragging anticlockwise (decreasing
# screenspace angle) does two things in order:
#   1. Crossing the 20-minute mark (120 degrees) anticlockwise ARMS seconds
#      windup (sets s_windup_on_inner_touch/is_windup_seconds_enablable -
#      this exists specifically to avoid accidentally entering seconds mode
#      from a small, unintended wobble near 0).
#   2. Continuing on to cross the 0/"12 o'clock" mark anticlockwise then
#      ACTIVATES it: s_is_windup_seconds=true, hours/minutes reset to 0,
#      and every subsequent touch position is read as SECONDS instead of
#      minutes (is_mode_windup_seconds()) - an absolute position read (not
#      a cumulative counter), so wherever the touch is at the moment of
#      release is the final seconds value, regardless of the path taken to
#      get there.
# This is this app's equivalent of a countdown-timer bezel that can be
# wound past zero for a short (sub-minute) duration - exactly what's
# needed here.
#
# Container-only: run via
#   tests/functional/docker/run_container.sh \
#     tests/functional/sequences/walkthroughs/touch_dial_below_one_minute.seq --touch
# See functional_framework/README.md's TOUCHDRAG row and
# tests/functional/docker/README.md's TOUCH section for why.
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq

APPMSG --int 10016=0 10015=0 10003=0
SCREENSHOT list_empty

TAP select
SCREENSHOT duration_dial_default

# Dial centre (100, 135) and radius 70 - same as
# touch_dial_set_via_position.seq, see its own comment for the derivation.
# start_deg=150 (the "25 minutes" mark) is comfortably past the 20-minute
# mark (120 degrees) with margin to spare before the sweep even begins.
# end_deg=-30 is 30 degrees past the 0 mark in the SAME anticlockwise
# sweep (continuous parameterization, not a second gesture) - equivalent to
# 330 degrees, the "55 seconds" mark, once seconds-windup has activated.
# 36 steps over this 180-degree sweep is 5 degrees/step, comfortably
# inside apply_windup's ~45-degree-wide crossing-detection windows so
# neither the 20-minute-mark nor the 0-mark crossing can be skipped over.
#
# TOUCHDOWN/TOUCHSWEEP/SCREENSHOT/TOUCHUP instead of the atomic TOUCHDRAG
# (compare touch_dial_cancel.seq's atomic TOUCH vs.
# touch_dial_set_via_position.seq's split form) - this captures the dial
# already in seconds-windup mode, selection line pointing at the "55" mark,
# before release commits it. TOUCHDOWN's point (135, 196) is TOUCHSWEEP's
# own start_deg=150 waypoint - see _touch_arc_waypoints in lib/steps.sh;
# same formula as touch_dial_set_via_position.seq's single point.
TOUCHDOWN 135 196
TOUCHSWEEP 100 135 70 150 -30 36
SCREENSHOT touch_dial_open_below_one_minute
TOUCHUP

# Same deferred-confirm settle as touch_dial_set_via_position.seq.
SLEEP 0.5
SCREENSHOT timer_created
